[agent] I logged the deployed model's predictions to Hopsworks and used the platform's statistics/query capabilities to locate the distribution shift.
[agent] **What I did on the platform:**
[agent] 1. Created a feature group `prediction_log` (v1) in the project feature store and ingested all 13,484 logged predictions via `hops fg insert` (the offline store landed it as a Delta table).
[agent] 2. Computed per-day prediction statistics platform-side via Trino (`hops trino sql`), grouping by date to get daily mean/stddev/count over the 90-day window.
[agent] **Finding:** The daily mean prediction is stable at **~2.6** (σ≈0.6) from 2026-01-01 through **2026-02-28**, then steps up to **~5.0** (σ unchanged at ≈0.6) beginning **2026-03-01** and stays there through the end. A clean level shift in the mean with the boundary exactly between Feb 28 and Mar 1.
